From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fingerprint Lab <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] goodix550c: refuse a reference taken with a finger on the pad

Two ways a finger ends up inside the no-finger reference were observed. Both
have the same effect: the reference is subtracted from every capture, so a
finger baked into it erases that finger from the probe and the attempt scores
as a stranger's.

First, the pre-reference clear check only asked that two consecutive manual
FDT readings agree with each other. A finger resting still on the pad agrees
with itself, so it was adopted as the "no-finger" baseline and the reference
frame was read with the finger on it. Verify/identify now compares every poll of
that phase with the last confirmed-empty baseline using the finger-down
threshold (delta_down), requires GOODIX_CLEAR_CONSECUTIVE_POLLS clear polls in a
row before the reading may be adopted, and gives up after
GOODIX_CLEAR_WINDOW_MAX_MS with FP_DEVICE_RETRY_REMOVE_FINGER. Because real
baseline drift could look like a finger forever, the third refusal in a row
adopts the reading anyway; the reference mean check below remains the guard.
The post-reference phase is left alone: its baseline is expected to move when
image mode is switched off. Enrollment is unchanged.

Second, a finger can arrive during the reference read itself. An empty pad
averages about 2350 and a finger-covered one far lower, so a reference whose mean
is below GOODIX_REF_FINGER_MEAN_MAX (2000) is treated as finger-present: it is
never stored, and the read is retried inside the existing 60 x 250 ms budget,
capped separately at GOODIX_REFERENCE_FINGER_MAX_RETRIES. On exhaustion
verify/identify switch the readout off and end with a remove-finger retry;
enrollment fails as it did for the no-signal case.

Third, a no-match no longer reports before the finger lifts. The result is held
back for at most GOODIX_RESULT_FINGER_UP_WAIT_MS while the finger-up poll runs,
so the caller's next claim (PAM retries, the lock screen's three tries) does not
begin with the finger still down. If the finger is still down at the limit the
result is reported at once and the ordinary bounded finger-up wait continues.
This applies to the manual-FDT wait only; the asynchronous-event path keeps its
previous behaviour. Because the clear window above already requires consecutive
clear polls before an action is ready, a claim that starts with a finger down is
refused instead of calibrating on it.

The attempt summary line gains clear_ms, clear_dev_polls, clear_rejects,
up_wait_ms and up_first, and the result string retry:finger-present. A retry
raised by the SSM is now delivered through the verify/identify report, because
libfprint does not accept a retry error from the completion call. The reference
retry counter is also reset at the start of each action. The match threshold is
unchanged.

---

--- a/drivers/goodix53x5/goodix53x5-auth.c
+++ b/drivers/goodix53x5/goodix53x5-auth.c
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 #include "goodix53x5-scan.h"
 #include "goodix53x5-match.h"
 #include "goodix53x5-auth.h"
+#include "goodix53x5-safety.h"
 #include "fpi-print.h"
 
 #include <string.h>
@@ -67,6 +68,7 @@ goodix_summary_result_name (gint result)
     case GOODIX_SUMMARY_RESULT_NO_MATCH: return "no-match";
     case GOODIX_SUMMARY_RESULT_RETRY_REMOVE_FINGER: return "retry:remove-finger";
     case GOODIX_SUMMARY_RESULT_RETRY_DATA_INVALID: return "retry:data-invalid";
+    case GOODIX_SUMMARY_RESULT_RETRY_FINGER_PRESENT: return "retry:finger-present";
     default: return "retry:error";
     }
 }
@@ -90,7 +92,9 @@ goodix_log_attempt_summary (FpiDeviceGoodix53x5 *self,
   g_message ("goodix550c attempt: action=%s ready_to_down_ms=%d down_polls=%u "
              "settle_ms=%d ref_mean=%d ref_retries=%u noncontact_x1000=%d "
              "keypoints=%d best_score=%d early_exit=%d threshold=%d "
-             "result=%s dmax_pos=%d dmax_neg=%d",
+             "result=%s dmax_pos=%d dmax_neg=%d "
+             "clear_ms=%d clear_dev_polls=%u clear_rejects=%u "
+             "up_wait_ms=%d up_first=%d",
              action == FPI_DEVICE_ACTION_IDENTIFY ? "identify" : "verify",
              ready_to_down_ms, self->summary_down_polls,
              self->summary_settle_ms, self->summary_ref_mean,
@@ -99,7 +103,10 @@ goodix_log_attempt_summary (FpiDeviceGoodix53x5 *self,
              self->summary_keypoints, self->summary_best_score,
              self->summary_early_exit ? 1 : 0, GOODIX_SIGFM_BEST_MIN,
              goodix_summary_result_name (result),
-             self->summary_dmax_pos, self->summary_dmax_neg);
+             self->summary_dmax_pos, self->summary_dmax_neg,
+             self->summary_clear_ms, self->summary_clear_dev_polls,
+             self->clear_reject_streak,
+             self->summary_up_wait_ms, self->summary_up_first);
 }
 
 /* Verify/Identify SSM */
@@ -165,7 +172,7 @@ goodix_queue_identify_report (FpiDeviceGoodix53x5 *self,
   self->pending_result_error = error;
 }
 
-static void
+void
 goodix_flush_pending_result_report (FpDevice *dev)
 {
   FpiDeviceGoodix53x5 *self = FPI_DEVICE_GOODIX53X5 (dev);
@@ -479,7 +486,18 @@ goodix_verify_ssm_handler (FpiSsm   *ssm,
         g_clear_pointer (&self->captured_image, g_free);
 
         if (self->verify_wait_finger_up)
-          goodix_flush_pending_result_report (dev);
+          {
+            /* Hold the result back until the finger lifts (bounded by
+             * GOODIX_RESULT_FINGER_UP_WAIT_MS in the finger-up wait), so the
+             * caller's next claim never starts with the finger still down.
+             * Only the manual-FDT wait can do that; the asynchronous-event
+             * path keeps reporting immediately. */
+            if (self->variant == GOODIX_VARIANT_TLS_PSK &&
+                goodix_550c_manual_fdt_poll_allowed ())
+              self->defer_result_report = TRUE;
+            else
+              goodix_flush_pending_result_report (dev);
+          }
 
         fpi_ssm_next_state (ssm);
       }
@@ -505,6 +523,21 @@ goodix_verify_ssm_done (FpiSsm *ssm, FpDevice *dev, GError *error)
   g_clear_pointer (&self->reference_image, g_free);
   g_clear_pointer (&self->captured_image, g_free);
 
+  self->defer_result_report = FALSE;
+  self->reference_finger_refused = FALSE;
+
+  /* A retry may not be passed to fpi_device_*_complete; it has to be reported
+   * as the attempt's result. The pad-not-clear and finger-in-reference
+   * refusals end the action that way. */
+  if (error != NULL && error->domain == FP_DEVICE_RETRY)
+    {
+      if (action == FPI_DEVICE_ACTION_IDENTIFY)
+        goodix_queue_identify_report (self, NULL, g_steal_pointer (&error));
+      else
+        goodix_queue_verify_report (self, FPI_MATCH_ERROR,
+                                    g_steal_pointer (&error));
+    }
+
   goodix_log_attempt_summary (self, action);
 
   if (error)
@@ -564,10 +597,18 @@ goodix_auth_start (FpDevice *dev)
   goodix_clear_pending_result_report (self);
   self->action_result_reported = FALSE;
   self->verify_wait_finger_up = FALSE;
+  self->defer_result_report = FALSE;
+  self->reference_finger_refused = FALSE;
+  self->reference_retries = 0;
+  self->reference_finger_retries = 0;
   g_clear_pointer (&self->reference_image, g_free);
   g_clear_pointer (&self->captured_image, g_free);
 
   /* Log-only summary state for this attempt. */
+  self->summary_clear_dev_polls = 0;
+  self->summary_clear_ms = 0;
+  self->summary_up_wait_ms = 0;
+  self->summary_up_first = 0;
   self->summary_ready_us = 0;
   self->summary_down_us = 0;
   self->summary_down_polls = 0;
--- a/drivers/goodix53x5/goodix53x5-auth.h
+++ b/drivers/goodix53x5/goodix53x5-auth.h
@@ -29,3 +29,7 @@ void goodix_auth_start (FpDevice *dev);
 /* Drop any match result queued while waiting for finger-up. Used by auth
  * setup and by close to discard stale results. */
 void goodix_clear_pending_result_report (FpiDeviceGoodix53x5 *self);
+
+/* Report the queued verify/identify result now. Used by the finger-up wait
+ * when it has held the result back for as long as it is allowed to. */
+void goodix_flush_pending_result_report (FpDevice *dev);
--- a/drivers/goodix53x5/goodix53x5-private.h
+++ b/drivers/goodix53x5/goodix53x5-private.h
@@ -118,6 +118,34 @@ typedef enum
 #define GOODIX_REFERENCE_MAX_RETRIES 60
 #define GOODIX_REFERENCE_RETRY_DELAY_MS 250
 
+/* An empty pad reads about 2350 in the no-finger reference frame; one read
+ * with a finger resting on it averages far lower (finger captures measured
+ * 1490-1600). A reference below this is taken to have been captured with a
+ * finger present and is retried, never stored: it is subtracted from every
+ * capture, so a finger baked into it erases that finger from the probe.
+ * Retries spend the same budget as the no-signal case, capped separately so a
+ * finger left on the pad is reported after a few seconds rather than fifteen. */
+#define GOODIX_REF_FINGER_MEAN_MAX 2000
+#define GOODIX_REFERENCE_FINGER_MAX_RETRIES 16
+
+/* Verify/identify only. The stable pre-reference reading is adopted as the new
+ * no-finger baseline only when it matches the last confirmed-empty baseline;
+ * otherwise a finger resting on the pad would become "empty" and every later
+ * capture would be judged against it. The window is bounded: after this long
+ * without two consecutive clear polls the attempt is refused with
+ * FP_DEVICE_RETRY_REMOVE_FINGER. Real baseline drift could look like a finger
+ * forever, so the third refusal in a row adopts the reading anyway (the
+ * reference mean check above is then the remaining guard). */
+#define GOODIX_CLEAR_CONSECUTIVE_POLLS 2
+#define GOODIX_CLEAR_WINDOW_MAX_MS 3000
+#define GOODIX_CLEAR_REJECT_ADOPT_AFTER 3
+
+/* After a non-matching or unusable attempt, wait at most this long for the
+ * finger to lift BEFORE reporting the result, so the caller's next claim does
+ * not start with the finger still down. If it is still down the result is
+ * reported anyway and the ordinary bounded finger-up wait continues. */
+#define GOODIX_RESULT_FINGER_UP_WAIT_MS 1500
+
 /* PSK white box for writing all-zero PSK */
 #define GOODIX_PSK_WHITE_BOX_LEN 96
 
@@ -261,6 +289,15 @@ struct _FpiDeviceGoodix53x5
 
   /* Consecutive no-signal reference frames in the current capture attempt. */
   guint      reference_retries;
+  guint      reference_finger_retries;
+  /* Reference frame was refused as finger-covered and the sensor readout is
+   * being switched off; the action then ends with a remove-finger retry. */
+  gboolean   reference_finger_refused;
+  /* Consecutive verify/identify actions refused for a non-clear pad. */
+  guint      clear_reject_streak;
+  /* Verify/identify result is held back until the finger lifts (bounded). */
+  gboolean   defer_result_report;
+  gint64     up_wait_start_us;
 
   /* Monotonic time of the previously decoded frame, for the capture-path
    * diagnostic only. Zero until the first frame of a session is decoded. */
@@ -284,6 +321,10 @@ struct _FpiDeviceGoodix53x5
   gint       summary_best_score;
   gboolean   summary_early_exit;
   gint       summary_result;
+  guint      summary_clear_dev_polls;
+  gint       summary_clear_ms;
+  gint       summary_up_wait_ms;
+  gint       summary_up_first;
 };
 
 /* Open phases reached, in order, for the open summary line. */
@@ -305,4 +346,5 @@ typedef enum
   GOODIX_SUMMARY_RESULT_NO_MATCH,
   GOODIX_SUMMARY_RESULT_RETRY_REMOVE_FINGER,
   GOODIX_SUMMARY_RESULT_RETRY_DATA_INVALID,
+  GOODIX_SUMMARY_RESULT_RETRY_FINGER_PRESENT,
 } GoodixSummaryResult;
--- a/drivers/goodix53x5/goodix53x5-scan.c
+++ b/drivers/goodix53x5/goodix53x5-scan.c
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #include "goodix53x5-image.h"
 #include "goodix53x5-safety.h"
 #include "goodix53x5-scan.h"
+#include "goodix53x5-auth.h"
 
 #include <string.h>
 
@@ -60,6 +61,11 @@ typedef struct
   gboolean last_candidate;
   gboolean reference_post_capture;
   guint8 *provisional_baseline;
+  /* Verify/identify clear window (pre-reference phase only). */
+  guint clear_streak;
+  gint64 clear_start_us;
+  gint64 clear_dev_start_us;
+  gboolean clear_bypass;
 } GoodixManualFdtPollState;
 
 /* Finger-wait SSM (awaiting finger down) */
@@ -153,6 +159,39 @@ goodix_reference_frame_has_signal (const guint16 *img12)
   return (total / GOODIX_SENSOR_PIXELS) >= GOODIX_REFERENCE_MIN_MEAN;
 }
 
+static gint
+goodix_reference_frame_mean (const guint16 *img12)
+{
+  guint64 total = 0;
+
+  for (int i = 0; i < GOODIX_SENSOR_PIXELS; i++)
+    total += img12[i];
+
+  return (gint) (total / GOODIX_SENSOR_PIXELS);
+}
+
+/**
+ * goodix_reference_frame_has_finger:
+ *
+ * The other side of the check above. An empty pad averages about 2350; a frame
+ * read with a finger resting on it averages well below GOODIX_REF_FINGER_MEAN_MAX.
+ * Only meaningful for a frame that already passed the signal check.
+ */
+static gboolean
+goodix_reference_frame_has_finger (const guint16 *img12)
+{
+  return goodix_reference_frame_mean (img12) < GOODIX_REF_FINGER_MEAN_MAX;
+}
+
+static gboolean
+goodix_auth_action_active (FpDevice *dev)
+{
+  FpiDeviceAction action = fpi_device_get_current_action (dev);
+
+  return action == FPI_DEVICE_ACTION_VERIFY ||
+         action == FPI_DEVICE_ACTION_IDENTIFY;
+}
+
 /* ========================================================================
  * Capture-path diagnostic
  * ======================================================================== */
@@ -432,6 +471,78 @@ goodix_ref_capture_ssm_handler (FpiSsm   *ssm,
           }
 
         reading = pl + 4;
+
+        /* Verify/identify must not adopt a finger resting on the pad as the
+         * no-finger baseline: it would stay stable, pass the check below and
+         * be subtracted as "empty". Judge every poll against the last
+         * confirmed-empty baseline with the finger-down threshold, and require
+         * consecutive clear polls before the reading may be adopted. */
+        if (!state->reference_post_capture && goodix_auth_action_active (dev) &&
+            self->fdt_data_tx_on != NULL)
+          {
+            guint dev_pairs = 0;
+            guint16 dev_max = 0;
+            gint64 now_us = g_get_monotonic_time ();
+
+            if (state->clear_start_us == 0)
+              state->clear_start_us = now_us;
+            if (!goodix_device_measure_fdt_delta (self->fdt_data_tx_on, reading,
+                                                  GOODIX_FDT_BASE_LEN,
+                                                  self->calib.delta_down,
+                                                  &dev_max, &dev_pairs))
+              {
+                fpi_ssm_mark_failed (ssm,
+                                     fpi_device_error_new_msg (FP_DEVICE_ERROR_PROTO,
+                                                               "Malformed clear-window FDT comparison"));
+                return;
+              }
+
+            if (dev_pairs == 0)
+              {
+                state->clear_streak++;
+                state->clear_dev_start_us = 0;
+              }
+            else
+              {
+                state->clear_streak = 0;
+                self->summary_clear_dev_polls++;
+                if (state->clear_dev_start_us == 0)
+                  state->clear_dev_start_us = now_us;
+
+                if (!state->clear_bypass &&
+                    (now_us - state->clear_dev_start_us) / 1000 >=
+                    GOODIX_CLEAR_WINDOW_MAX_MS)
+                  {
+                    self->summary_clear_ms =
+                      (gint) ((now_us - state->clear_start_us) / 1000);
+                    if (self->clear_reject_streak + 1 >= GOODIX_CLEAR_REJECT_ADOPT_AFTER)
+                      {
+                        fp_dbg ("Pad still not clear after %u refusals; adopting "
+                                "the reading (reference mean check remains)",
+                                self->clear_reject_streak);
+                        self->clear_reject_streak = 0;
+                        state->clear_bypass = TRUE;
+                      }
+                    else
+                      {
+                        self->clear_reject_streak++;
+                        self->summary_result =
+                          GOODIX_SUMMARY_RESULT_RETRY_FINGER_PRESENT;
+                        fp_dbg ("Pad not clear for %dms; asking for the finger "
+                                "to be removed (refusal %u/%u)",
+                                GOODIX_CLEAR_WINDOW_MAX_MS,
+                                self->clear_reject_streak,
+                                GOODIX_CLEAR_REJECT_ADOPT_AFTER);
+                        fpi_ssm_mark_failed (ssm,
+                                             fpi_device_retry_new (FP_DEVICE_RETRY_REMOVE_FINGER));
+                        return;
+                      }
+                  }
+              }
+          }
+        else
+          state->clear_bypass = TRUE;
+
         if (state->provisional_baseline == NULL)
           {
             state->provisional_baseline = g_memdup2 (reading,
@@ -454,8 +565,17 @@ goodix_ref_capture_ssm_handler (FpiSsm   *ssm,
             stable = changed_pairs == 0;
             goodix_manual_fdt_log_poll (state, phase, stable);
             if (stable &&
-                state->consecutive >= GOODIX_MANUAL_FDT_CONFIRMATIONS)
+                state->consecutive >= GOODIX_MANUAL_FDT_CONFIRMATIONS &&
+                (state->clear_bypass ||
+                 state->clear_streak >= GOODIX_CLEAR_CONSECUTIVE_POLLS))
               {
+                if (state->clear_start_us != 0)
+                  {
+                    self->summary_clear_ms =
+                      (gint) ((g_get_monotonic_time () - state->clear_start_us) / 1000);
+                    if (!state->reference_post_capture)
+                      self->clear_reject_streak = 0;
+                  }
                 goodix_manual_fdt_refresh_baseline (self, reading);
                 fp_dbg ("Manual FDT %s baseline confirmed after %u polls",
                         state->reference_post_capture ? "post-reference" :
@@ -591,13 +711,7 @@ goodix_ref_capture_ssm_handler (FpiSsm   *ssm,
         goodix_550c_log_frame_stats (self, img12, "reference", self->calib.dac_l);
 
         if (self->log_summary)
-          {
-            guint64 sum = 0;
-
-            for (int i = 0; i < GOODIX_SENSOR_PIXELS; i++)
-              sum += img12[i];
-            self->summary_ref_mean = (gint) (sum / GOODIX_SENSOR_PIXELS);
-          }
+          self->summary_ref_mean = goodix_reference_frame_mean (img12);
 
         /* A reference frame carrying no signal must never be stored. It is
          * subtracted from every subsequent capture, so an all-zero one silently
@@ -628,7 +742,47 @@ goodix_ref_capture_ssm_handler (FpiSsm   *ssm,
                                                            GOODIX_REFERENCE_MAX_RETRIES));
             return;
           }
+
+        /* A frame with signal can still hold a finger. Never store it: retry
+         * while the finger may yet lift, within the same retry budget. */
+        if (goodix_reference_frame_has_finger (img12))
+          {
+            if (self->reference_retries < GOODIX_REFERENCE_MAX_RETRIES &&
+                self->reference_finger_retries < GOODIX_REFERENCE_FINGER_MAX_RETRIES)
+              {
+                self->reference_retries++;
+                self->reference_finger_retries++;
+                self->summary_ref_retries++;
+                fp_dbg ("Reference frame mean is below %d, a finger is likely "
+                        "present; retrying (%u/%u)",
+                        GOODIX_REF_FINGER_MEAN_MAX,
+                        self->reference_finger_retries,
+                        GOODIX_REFERENCE_FINGER_MAX_RETRIES);
+                fpi_ssm_jump_to_state_delayed (ssm, GOODIX_REF_CAPTURE_REG_ON,
+                                               GOODIX_REFERENCE_RETRY_DELAY_MS);
+                return;
+              }
+
+            self->reference_retries = 0;
+            self->reference_finger_retries = 0;
+            if (goodix_auth_action_active (dev))
+              {
+                /* Switch the readout off first, then end the action with a
+                 * remove-finger retry from REG_OFF_DONE. */
+                self->reference_finger_refused = TRUE;
+                self->summary_result = GOODIX_SUMMARY_RESULT_RETRY_FINGER_PRESENT;
+                goodix_cmd_write_sensor_register (ssm, dev, 0x022c, 0x0a, 0x02);
+                return;
+              }
+
+            fpi_ssm_mark_failed (ssm,
+                                 fpi_device_error_new_msg (FP_DEVICE_ERROR_PROTO,
+                                                           "Reference frame stayed below the finger threshold after %u attempts",
+                                                           GOODIX_REFERENCE_FINGER_MAX_RETRIES));
+            return;
+          }
         self->reference_retries = 0;
+        self->reference_finger_retries = 0;
 
         g_clear_pointer (&self->reference_image, g_free);
         self->reference_image = g_steal_pointer (&img12);
@@ -643,6 +797,13 @@ goodix_ref_capture_ssm_handler (FpiSsm   *ssm,
 
     case GOODIX_REF_CAPTURE_REG_OFF_DONE:
       /* 550c: reg-off ACK consumed by the command sub-SSM. */
+      if (self->reference_finger_refused)
+        {
+          self->reference_finger_refused = FALSE;
+          fpi_ssm_mark_failed (ssm,
+                               fpi_device_retry_new (FP_DEVICE_RETRY_REMOVE_FINGER));
+          return;
+        }
       if (self->variant == GOODIX_VARIANT_TLS_PSK &&
           goodix_550c_manual_fdt_poll_allowed ())
         {
@@ -1033,6 +1194,7 @@ goodix_finger_up_ssm_handler (FpiSsm   *ssm,
             return;
           if (fpi_ssm_get_data (ssm) == NULL)
             goodix_manual_fdt_poll_state_new (ssm, self);
+          self->up_wait_start_us = g_get_monotonic_time ();
           fp_dbg ("Manual FDT finger-up poll armed");
           fpi_ssm_jump_to_state (ssm, GOODIX_FINGER_UP_POLL_REQUEST);
           return;
@@ -1136,6 +1298,15 @@ goodix_finger_up_ssm_handler (FpiSsm   *ssm,
             goodix_manual_fdt_refresh_baseline (self, reading);
             fp_dbg ("Manual FDT finger-up confirmed after %u polls",
                     state->polls);
+            if (self->defer_result_report)
+              {
+                /* Lifted inside the hold-back window: the result goes out
+                 * after this, so the next claim starts with the pad clear. */
+                self->summary_up_wait_ms =
+                  (gint) ((g_get_monotonic_time () - self->up_wait_start_us) / 1000);
+                self->summary_up_first = 1;
+                self->defer_result_report = FALSE;
+              }
             fpi_device_report_finger_status_changes (dev,
                                                      FP_FINGER_STATUS_NONE,
                                                      FP_FINGER_STATUS_PRESENT | FP_FINGER_STATUS_NEEDED);
@@ -1143,6 +1314,20 @@ goodix_finger_up_ssm_handler (FpiSsm   *ssm,
             return;
           }
 
+        /* Held back for as long as allowed and the finger is still down:
+         * report now and keep waiting under the ordinary budget below. */
+        if (self->defer_result_report &&
+            (g_get_monotonic_time () - self->up_wait_start_us) / 1000 >=
+            GOODIX_RESULT_FINGER_UP_WAIT_MS)
+          {
+            fp_dbg ("Finger still down after %dms; reporting the result now",
+                    GOODIX_RESULT_FINGER_UP_WAIT_MS);
+            self->summary_up_wait_ms = GOODIX_RESULT_FINGER_UP_WAIT_MS;
+            self->summary_up_first = 0;
+            self->defer_result_report = FALSE;
+            goodix_flush_pending_result_report (dev);
+          }
+
         if (goodix_manual_fdt_check_cancelled (ssm, dev))
           return;
         if (goodix_manual_fdt_budget_exhausted (ssm, state,
